# Restaurant Admin Dashboard Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Build a comprehensive operational dashboard for restaurant partners to manage orders (Kanban), curate menus (Visual Editor), and track business growth (Analytics).

**Architecture:** A specialized admin la-section of the web app. It uses a role-based access control (RBAC) guard to restrict access. Real-time order updates are handled via Socket.io, while menu and analytics data are managed via REST API endpoints.

**Tech Stack:** Next.js 14, React, Tailwind CSS, Socket.io-client, Lucide React, Recharts (for analytics).

---

## File Structure

- Create: `apps/web/src/pages/admin/dashboard.tsx` - Main admin entry point and RBAC guard.
- Create: `apps/web/src/pages/admin/orders.tsx` - Kanban board for order management.
- Create: `apps/web/src/components/admin/OrderKanban.tsx` - Drag-and-drop order board logic.
- Create: `apps/web/src/components/admin/OrderDetailsPanel.tsx` - Side-panel for detailed order view.
- Create: `apps/web/src/pages/admin/menu.tsx` - Visual menu editor.
- Create: `apps/web/src/components/admin/MenuCard.tsx` - Individual item editor with "Out of Stock" toggle.
- Create: `apps/web/src/pages/admin/analytics.tsx` - Data visualization dashboard.
- Create: `apps/web/src/components/admin/AnalyticsCharts.tsx` - Revenue and popularity charts using Recharts.

